# IMP Parallelism Policy

Use **one agent** by default. More agents is not better execution.

Parallelize only when the work is genuinely independent and parallel execution
materially improves speed or coverage without meaningful coordination,
architectural, evidence, or Git-state risk.

Do **not** create agents merely because parallel agents are available.

**Owner:** every task has exactly one primary owner. Subagents own only a
bounded lane. The primary owns final architecture, integration, validation,
canonical Git state, and the final report.

**Mutable state:** multiple agents must not concurrently mutate the same
working tree. Parallel implementation uses separate worktrees/branches with
file ownership; the primary integrates afterward. Read-only audits may share
a tree.

Do not parallelize when tasks share files, order/architecture is undecided,
evidence-sensitive runtime/schedulers are involved, or one agent is not a
bottleneck.

Workflow: skill `imp-agent-orchestration`. Worktrees: `docs/engineering/sops/GIT_WORKTREE.md`.
